        "b_publish": {
          "type": "band",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What we publish",
            "body": "<p>For every product, the full picture is on the page. Each ingredient appears under its INCI name, the standardised name used on labels the world over, with a plain-English name alongside so you are not left translating Latin. The list runs in order of weight, most abundant first, and we carry that order all the way down to the smallest trace, which goes further than the labelling rules require. Beside each one sits its exact percentage.</p><p>We also mark how ingredients are made. A star means organic. A caret means cold-pressed. Most of the plant oils carry both. A hash means upcycled, made from a by-product of another process. And where there is an aromatic in the formula, it is named outright as vetiver, never folded into a vague \"parfum\" or \"fragrance\".</p>",
            "variant": "plain",
            "set_piece": "mark_legend",
            "ethos_icon": "none",
            "mark_1": "organic",
