        "b_howread": {
          "type": "band",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to read a Biotaderm formulation",
            "body": "<p>It is simpler than it looks. The order is the key: ingredients are listed from most to least, so whatever sits near the top makes up the bulk of the product, and the actives you have read about usually sit lower down, where small amounts are normal. Each line gives you the INCI name, the everyday name in brackets, and the percentage. A star after a name means organic, a caret means cold-pressed, and a hash means upcycled. The short legend at the foot of every list spells it out. That is the whole code.</p>",
